Dear Professor Lesage,

On behalf of the European Research Executive Agency, I am pleased to inform you that the
Laboratoire LIAV of the Université de Valmont has been identified as a prospective
beneficiary of the Doctoral Network EFFICIENT-HPC, to be established under the Marie
Skłodowska-Curie Actions of Horizon Europe.

The network, coordinated by the University of Aldergate, will train fourteen doctoral
candidates across eight beneficiaries, including the Universidade de Lisboa Boavista
(Portugal), TU Heldring (Netherlands) and IRIS Saint-Martin. Its research programme -
energy-aware and trustworthy high-performance computing - is directly aligned with the
activities of your laboratory.

As a prospective beneficiary, the LIAV would host two doctoral candidates and co-supervise
a third with Kerdata as industrial partner. The complete proposal is scheduled for
submission on 9 February 2027.

I attach for your information the draft letter of intent. Should your laboratory wish to
participate, we kindly ask you to return the countersigned letter before 15 November
2026, to the attention of the network coordinator.

For any question regarding the scientific programme of the network, the coordinator
remains at your disposal.

Yours faithfully,

Dr. Annika Sørensen
Project Officer - Doctoral Networks Unit
European Research Executive Agency (EREA)

